</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000064N00DX_04_0023" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000064N00DX_04_0010" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064N00DX_04_0023" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CAO00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Distance Control Computer Assembly (IGB Terminal, SGND Terminal, LRDD Terminal)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect the distance control computer assembly connector.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Make sure that the millimeter wave radar sensor assembly connector is disconnected.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn IG ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between the terminals of the distance control computer assembly connector. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM00000064800HX"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E104768J19" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>13(IGB) - 10(SGND)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>11 to 14 V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between the terminals of the distance control computer assembly connector. (see <xref label="Seep03" href="RM00000064800HX"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E104768J20" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>22(LRDD) - 10(SGND)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4.5 to 5.5 V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten3>
<ptxt>DTCs may be detected when connectors are disconnected for inspection. Therefore, be sure to clear the DTCs using TaSCAN after completing the inspection.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000064N00DX_04_0031" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM00000064N00DX_04_0028" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064N00DX_04_0031" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CAQ00000">
<testtitle>Replace Millimeter Wave Radar Sensor Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Replace the millimeter wave radar sensor assembly with a new one.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform radar axis adjustment of the millimeter wave radar sensor assembly. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000028Z6003X"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000064N00DX_04_0033" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064N00DX_04_0033" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CHZ00000">
<testtitle>Clear DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), clear the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000064C00EX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000064N00DX_04_0024" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064N00DX_04_0024" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CAP00000">
<testtitle>Check DTCs (Radar Cruise Control System)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Put the vehicle in the conditions under which the DTC is detected.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>The system cannot detect the malfunction unless the detection conditions are met.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<test2>
<ptxt>Drive within the cruise control set vehicle speed range.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Turn the cruise control main switch ON and put the system in vehicle-to-vehicle distance control mode standby.</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), check the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000064C00EX"/>)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.89in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.24in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>U0235 is not output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>U0235 is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM00000064N00DX_04_0032" fin="true">A</down>
<right ref="RM00000064N00DX_04_0008" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064N00DX_04_0032">
<testtitle>Complete</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM00000064N00DX_04_0008">
<testtitle>Replace Distance Control Computer Assembly<xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000028Z2003X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
